    "content": "<!-- wp:cil/hero {\"sub\":\"Two experienced practitioners who have trained UK and International doctors. Local anaesthetic every time.\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eCircumcision in London at Beverley Clinic provides male circumcision for infants, babies, children, teenagers, boys and adult men. Our two circumcision practitioners have more than 40 years of combined experience in the UK and abroad and have carried out thousands of successful circumcisions across all age groups.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe understand that choosing circumcision for yourself or your child is an important decision. Our aim is to explain the procedure clearly, answer your questions and support you from the initial enquiry through to aftercare and healing.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eCircumcision may be requested for religious (such as Muslim and Jewish), cultural, personal or medical reasons. Every patient is assessed individually, and the method used depends on age, anatomy and clinical circumstances.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cul\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eCQC registered clinic in North-West London\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eMore than 40 years of combined practitioner experience\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eCircumcision for babies, children, teenagers and adults\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eLocal anaesthetic used for circumcisions, with the area checked before the procedure begins\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003ePlastibell / Circumplast ring method commonly used for babies and toddlers\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eForceps-guided (traditional) method with thermal cautery commonly used for older children and adults\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eWritten aftercare information and preparation videos\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eNext-day follow-up call\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eFree follow-up appointments during the healing period\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eGP letter available to update medical records\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eSchool or work letters available where appropriate\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eEnglish, Arabic, Urdu, Hindi, Punjabi and Turkish spoken\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003c/ul\\u003e\",\"facts\":[],\"eyebrow\":\"CQC registered Ã‚Â· Edgware, North-West London\",\"title\":\"Dedicated Circumcision Clinic in London\",\"ctaLabel\":\"Book online\",\"ctaUrl\":\"http://circumcision-london-wp.local/book/\",\"phoneLabel\":\"Call 020 8951 3794\",\"phoneUrl\":\"tel:+442089513794\",\"showFacts\":true} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/groups {\"items\":[{\"href\":\"http://circumcision-london-wp.local/babies/\",\"title\":\"Babies and toddlers\",\"age\":\"Best under one month old\",\"price\":\"From Ã‚Â£200\",\"cta\":\"Baby circumcision, from Ã‚Â£200\",\"blurb\":\"Circumcision is commonly carried out using the Plastibell or Circumplast ring method. For young babies, the procedure itself is usually less than 10 minutes and no stitches are required with the ring method. Bath him straight away.\"},{\"href\":\"http://circumcision-london-wp.local/children/\",\"title\":\"Children and teenagers\",\"age\":\"One to seventeen years\",\"price\":\"From Ã‚Â£300\",\"cta\":\"Circumcision for boys, from Ã‚Â£300\",\"blurb\":\"Older children are commonly treated using the forceps-guided traditional method with thermal cautery resulting in minimal bleeding. We explain the procedure in an age-appropriate way and provide parents with detailed aftercare instructions.\"},{\"href\":\"http://circumcision-london-wp.local/adults/\",\"title\":\"Adults\",\"age\":\"Eighteen and over\",\"price\":\"From Ã‚Â£680\",\"cta\":\"Adult circumcision, from Ã‚Â£680\",\"blurb\":\"We provide adult circumcision for religious, cultural, personal and medical reasons, including foreskin problems such as phimosis, paraphimosis, balanitis and BXO. We also assess patients seeking re-circumcision or revision procedures.\"}]} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/trust-strip /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/process {\"eyebrow\":\"\",\"heading\":\"Next steps\",\"lede\":\"\",\"items\":[{\"h\":\"Contact us\",\"p\":\"Ask questions by telephone, WhatsApp or the website enquiry form.\"},{\"h\":\"Preparation\",\"p\":\"We send you written and video information to prepare you on what to bring, what to expect on the day and the expected aftercare following the circumcision.\"},{\"h\":\"Procedure\",\"p\":\"Local anaesthetic is given and the area is checked before the procedure begins.\"},{\"h\":\"Aftercare\",\"p\":\"You leave with written instructions. We contact you the following day to answer any further questions you may have and offer follow-up appointments during healing if needed.\"}]} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/home-callback {\"eyebrow\":\"\",\"heading\":\"When we may postpone\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003eWho is suitable for circumcision?\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe circumcise males of all ages and backgrounds, so whether it is for religious, cultural or medical reasons, we have you covered. Let us know when booking what your main reason for circumcising and we will accommodate you accordingly.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eOur 2 practitioners are Muslim and we treat a big portion of the Muslim community in London and from other parts of the UK. We also get patients from the Jewish community coming in for religious circumcisions.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eSome patients get circumcised to meet cultural requirements such as Filipinos, certain parts of Africa, Fiji and other countries where circumcision is an important part of their culture.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe also get a big portion of patients who have a medical reason for getting circumcised, most common is a tight foreskin (phimosis and paraphimosis), inflammation of the head of the penis (balanitis) as well as short and scarred frenulum.\\u003c/p\\u003e\",\"urgentTitle\":\"Urgent symptoms\",\"urgentBody\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eSeek urgent medical assessment if a pulled-back foreskin is trapped behind the head of the penis and swelling, if the patient cannot pass urine, or if there is spreading redness with fever. These symptoms should not wait for a routine clinic appointment and you should contact 999.\\u003c/p\\u003e\",\"cardHtml\":\"\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003eWant to ask before you book?\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe often call you back within a few minutes, but always within the same day even during busy times. Monday Ã¢â‚¬â€œ Saturday 09:00Ã¢â‚¬â€œ17:00.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003eName, phone number\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003ePatient DOB\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003eAnything you would like us to know (optional)\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\",\"cardTitle\":\"Ask before you book\",\"cardEyebrow\":\"Request a call back\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/intro {\"eyebrow\":\"\",\"heading\":\"Location\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eBeverley Clinic, 78 Beverley Drive, Edgware, HA8 5NE. The clinic is in North-West London with nearby public transport links and plenty of free street parking. Queensbury Underground station (8 mins walk) on the Jubilee line and Burnt Oak station on the Northern line (20 mins walk) are both nearby.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/reviews {\"body\":\"Most of our patients arrive because somebody they trust sent them. The families who come back are the part we are proudest of: some return after many years whenever there is a new son, others bring a brother, then a nephew, then a cousin. We have families we have now seen across three children and the better part of a decade.\",\"quotes\":[{\"name\":\"Mustafa Butt\",\"context\":\"Baby circumcision, three weeks old\",\"quote\":\"The receptionist explained the procedure clearly and put us at ease straight away. The doctor was thorough and professional, explained everything beforehand, and stayed calm and reassuring throughout. He took the time to go through the aftercare in detail.\"},{\"name\":\"Wajahat Murtaza\",\"context\":\"Baby circumcision\",\"quote\":\"Smooth and efficient from start to finish. Dr Haidar is professional and experienced, we were given all the information we needed, and a follow-up call was made as well, which is a nice thing to do. The ring came off after a week and my son is doing well.\"},{\"name\":\"Sara Salmanpour\",\"context\":\"Baby circumcision, two months old\",\"quote\":\"As first-time parents we were naturally anxious, but the team made us feel completely at ease. The doctor explained the procedure in detail and answered every concern with patience. They gave us the option to contact them any time afterwards, which was a huge relief.\"}]} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-warm\",\"anchor\":\"our-clinics\"} -->\n<section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-warm\" id=\"our-clinics\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"Our clinics\",\"heading\":\"London, Luton, Southampton and Birmingham\",\"lede\":\"The London clinic in Edgware can be booked online. Luton, Southampton and Birmingham are booked by telephone.\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"items\":[{\"eyebrow\":\"London\",\"title\":\"London Ã¢â‚¬â€ Edgware\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp style=\\u0022margin-top:12px\\u0022\\u003eBeverley Clinic\\u003cbr\\u003e78 Beverley Drive, Edgware HA8 5NE\\u003c/p\\u003e\",\"ctaLabel\":\"Book a consultation\",\"ctaUrl\":\"http://circumcision-london-wp.local/book/\",\"ctaClass\":\"btn\",\"cta2Label\":\"View London clinic\",\"cta2Url\":\"http://circumcision-london-wp.local/contact/\",\"cta2Class\":\"btn btn-ghost\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Luton\",\"title\":\"Luton\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp style=\\u0022margin-top:12px\\u0022\\u003eBeverley Clinic\\u003cbr\\u003eLiverpool Road Health Centre\\u003cbr\\u003eLuton LU1 1HH\\u003c/p\\u003e\",\"ctaLabel\":\"View Luton clinic\",\"ctaUrl\":\"http://circumcision-london-wp.local/luton-circumcision-clinic/\",\"ctaClass\":\"btn btn-ghost\",\"cta2Label\":\"\",\"cta2Url\":\"\",\"cta2Class\":\"btn btn-ghost\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Southampton\",\"title\":\"Southampton\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp style=\\u0022margin-top:12px\\u0022\\u003eBeverley Clinic\\u003cbr\\u003eEastleigh Health Centre\\u003cbr\\u003eEastleigh SO50 9AG\\u003c/p\\u003e\",\"ctaLabel\":\"View Southampton clinic\",\"ctaUrl\":\"http://circumcision-london-wp.local/southampton-circumcision-clinic/\",\"ctaClass\":\"btn btn-ghost\",\"cta2Label\":\"\",\"cta2Url\":\"\",\"cta2Class\":\"btn btn-ghost\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Birmingham\",\"title\":\"Birmingham\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp style=\\u0022margin-top:12px\\u0022\\u003eBeverley Clinic\\u003cbr\\u003eSoho Health Centre\\u003cbr\\u003eLouise Road\\u003cbr\\u003eBirmingham B21 9RY\\u003c/p\\u003e\",\"ctaLabel\":\"View Birmingham clinic\",\"ctaUrl\":\"http://circumcision-london-wp.local/birmingham-circumcision-clinic/\",\"ctaClass\":\"btn btn-ghost\",\"cta2Label\":\"\",\"cta2Url\":\"\",\"cta2Class\":\"btn btn-ghost\"}],\"columns\":\"g-4\",\"headingLevel\":2} /--></div></section>\n<!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/cta-band /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/faq {\"heading\":\"The questions we are asked most\",\"items\":[{\"q\":\"Is the circumcision painful?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eNo. Every patient has local anaesthetic, at every age. It is safe, and it is illegal to circumcise without it.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eWe do not simply assume it has worked. Once it has had time, we test the area and show you that no pain is felt, and we only begin once you tell us you are happy to proceed. Babies sometimes cry anyway: the anaesthetic removes pain but keeps ordinary touch sensation, which is painless, and an unfamiliar touch there is enough to make a baby object.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"How long does it take?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eFor a baby, the circumcision itself is about ten minutes, and the anaesthetic lasts around two hours afterwards. Older children and adults take longer. Allow about an hour for the visit either way, which covers the consultation, consent, the anaesthetic working and going through aftercare before you leave.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Which method do you use?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eFor babies and toddlers, we often use the ring method (e.g. Plastibell or Circumplast). The advantages are that it does not require any stitches, you can bath your son normally and often comes off by itself within 3-14 days similar to the umbilical cord. The disadvantages is that it sometimes does not come off automatically and will require us to remove it but this often takes less than 5 seconds.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eOlder children and adults are often circumcised with the forceps guided (traditional) method using thermal cautery which seals as it cuts, resulting in minimal bleeding if any. We close the wound using skin glue, stitches or a combination of both depending on the individual patient. Both of these come off naturally.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"What is the best age?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eUnder one month old, if the choice is open to you. At that age it is quick and simple and healing is faster. We circumcise routinely at every age after that, right through to adults, so it is never too late.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Do you carry out religious circumcision?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eYes, and it is a large part of what we do. Our Muslim practitioners carry out the procedure according to the Sunnah, and we routinely cater for all faiths and backgrounds. \\u003ca href=\\u0022http://circumcision-london-wp.local/religious/\\u0022\\u003eMore about religious and cultural circumcision\\u003c/a\\u003e.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Can you correct a circumcision done elsewhere?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eYes. Parents bring sons to us from across the UK and from abroad to tidy up work done somewhere else, and adults come for the same reason. It ranges from scar revision to tightening a loose result. \\u003ca href=\\u0022http://circumcision-london-wp.local/re-circumcision/\\u0022\\u003eMore about re-circumcision\\u003c/a\\u003e.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Do I need to do anything to prepare?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eVery little, because it is done under local anaesthetic. There is no fasting. When you book we send you videos on how to prepare and what to expect from start to finish, and the page for your age group lists exactly what to bring.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Could the NHS do this instead?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eWhere there is a medical need, yes, and if you can wait that is a reasonable choice. From what our patients tell us, the wait runs beyond a year. Religious and cultural circumcision is not funded. Give us a call if you would like to discuss further.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"}]} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
}
